cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "To cite these seals, please use the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "Forecast seals: survey waves and official statistics, 2026"
authors:
  - name: "Nate Grotberg"
abstract: >-
  Seal files for model-generated forecasts of nine survey waves: the 2026 General Social
  Survey and the 2026 Cooperative Election Study, sealed on 2026-09-07 and submitted to
  OpenTimestamps on 2026-09-23, and seven federal surveys (HTOPS November 2026, NHIS 2026,
  SHED 2026, BRFSS 2026, and the CPS ASEC, Computer and Internet Use, and Civic Engagement
  and Volunteering supplements of 2027), sealed and timestamped on 2026-11-06. Each seal is
  a sha256 digest over every forecast row for one survey wave (protocol forecast-seal-1).
  The repository also holds forward seals of recurring survey readings and series seals of
  official statistics. The repository includes the OpenTimestamps proofs and a
  standard-library Python verifier. The forecasts are model-generated predictions, not
  measurements.
keywords:
  - forecast
  - timestamping
  - OpenTimestamps
  - General Social Survey
  - Cooperative Election Study
  - Household Pulse Survey
  - National Health Interview Survey
  - Survey of Household Economics and Decisionmaking
  - Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System
  - Current Population Survey
